/* the melody pane: the pianoroll of a 303-style line, 16, 32 or 64 steps long, one pitch per step.
 *
 * It is a track of the sequencer view (a hidden pane owned by a VCO or a MIDI synth) and plays that object with the
 * transport. The grid shows one bar (16 steps) at a time on the shared step columns, so it lines up with the drum grid;
 * the page tabs move through the bars and `Follow` keeps the playing bar on screen.
 *
 *   Header 1  Len (16/32/64; a longer line starts as a repeat)  Root  Scale  Oct -/+ (the window of rows)
 *   Header 2  pages  Follow  rotate < >  transpose -1 +1  Dice (a new line within the scale; on a generated pattern
 *             the next take of its style, over the shown phrase's chords)  Aid  the bar's chord
 *   Aid       rows of the chord of the shown bar (the SONG view's chord row) light up: its root and tones in yellow, the
 *             key's blue note in blue; the other rows stay as they are. Off: plain rows
 *   Grid      rows are the scale's notes over one octave and the root above; touch a cell to set the note, touch the note
 *             again to clear it; drag across columns to paint, up and down to move the note
 *   Strips    ACC accent (louder, opens the filter), SLD slide (glides, holds the note), GATE (short/normal/long),
 *             PROB (the chance the step plays); touch toggles or cycles, drag paints
 *
 * Notes outside the window show as an arrow at its edge. The line lives in the song store (kind 'melody').
 */

